  "reading": "At the headline cell (biencoder_plus_ce + typed), none of step_f1, ordered_step_accuracy, rouge_l_f1, exact_match or composite_score differ significantly between any pair of the 3 pool-construction strategies (all bootstrap CIs cross 0, all paired t-tests p>0.1 except one borderline 0.038-0.044 pair on hop_count). The one significant axis is hop_count_exact_match_rate: imbalanced (0.5133) and clustered (0.5133, exactly tied) both significantly beat balanced (0.4667) by McNemar (p=0.044, p=0.038) and paired t-test (p=0.038, p=0.033); imbalanced vs clustered are statistically indistinguishable (identical rate, p=1.0). Per-hop, the gap is concentrated at hop=2 (imbalanced 0.756 / clustered 0.716 vs balanced 0.584) and persists at hop=3 in clustered's favour (0.552 vs imbalanced 0.472 vs balanced 0.504); all three strategies converge to similarly low hop=4 accuracy (0.27-0.31, the smallest pool bucket in every strategy). Reading: pool-construction strategy moves whether the model states the right STEP COUNT, not whether the steps it emits are the right ones (step_f1/ordered_step_accuracy unmoved) - the same shape exp-005 and exp-009 found on unrelated axes (oracle hop guidance, hop-matched retrieval). No claim is made that clustering beats imbalanced: they are indistinguishable here, and both beat balanced only on this one axis.",

